\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\qc\ul\b\f0\fs44\lang9 AIR POLLUTION MONITORING SYSTEM\ulnone\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
Introduction\par
\b0\fs32 Air pollution is one of the major environmental and public health problems caused by the presence of harmful gases, particulate matter, smoke, and other pollutants in the atmosphere. Rapid industrialization, increasing numbers of vehicles, construction activities, burning of fossil fuels, and improper waste disposal are major contributors to air pollution.\par
The proposed Air Pollution Monitoring System is designed to monitor air-quality parameters using suitable gas and particulate-matter sensors. The collected sensor data can be processed using a microcontroller and displayed locally or transmitted to an online platform for remote monitoring. The system can also generate alerts when pollution levels exceed predefined limits.\par
\b\fs40 Problem Statement\par
\b0\fs32 Air pollution is increasing because of vehicles, industries, construction work, and burning of waste. Polluted air can cause health problems and harm the environment. Many existing air pollution monitoring systems are expensive and are available only in limited places.\par
\b\fs40 Aim\par
\b0\fs32 To design and develop a real-time air pollution monitoring system capable of measuring important air-quality parameters and providing pollution-level information to users.\par
\b\fs40 Objectives\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\fs32 To measure the pollution level in the air.\par
