\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\fs40 Working Principle\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b0\fs32 The air-quality sensors continuously sense pollutants present in the surrounding atmosphere. The sensor signals are read by the microcontroller at regular intervals. The controller processes the readings and determines the corresponding pollution levels.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The measured values are displayed to the user. In an IoT-based implementation, the readings are also uploaded to a cloud server through a wireless network. Users can therefore monitor air quality remotely.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}If any parameter crosses its predefined threshold, the system activates an alert. The recorded data can  be analyzed to understand pollution trends and identify periods of poor air quality\b\fs40\par

